  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Florida has received $27.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government executed 179,318 awards in Florida, with an average award size of $155K. Obligations in Florida are down 14.1% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations moved from $25.7B in FY21 to $26.6B in FY22, $29B in FY23, $31.3B in FY24, $32.4B in FY25, and $27.9B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in Florida, obligating $18.3B so far in FY2026 to date. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations, totaling $5.2B in FY2026 to date. The state’s vendor list includes large obligations to LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $2.7B and $2.3B, THALLE CONSTRUCTION CO INC at $1.9B, and LOYAL SOURCE GOVERNMENT SERVICES LLC at $1.8B. This mix of large defense buys, space-sector manufacturing, construction, and healthcare services shapes federal contracting activity in Florida in the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive federal spending in Florida?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $18.3B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $2.8B, and the General Services Administration obligates $1.8B. Other significant buyers are the Department of Homeland Security and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration, each obligating $1.3B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries dominate contracts in Florida?",
        "body": "LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION is the largest vendor by obligations, with entries of $2.7B and $2.3B. THALLE CONSTRUCTION CO INC obligates $1.9B and LOYAL SOURCE GOVERNMENT SERVICES LLC obligates $1.8B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing leads industries with $5.2B, followed by Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $2.3B and Engineering Services at $2B."
      }
    ]
